; Binders range over terms (decided 2026-10-20): `∀`, `∃` (and every other binder) bind a term
; variable, never a statement. A statement variable is schematic: free in a `use` or `show`, `%A`
; says "for every statement" -- `use %A ∨ ¬%A`. Before, `∀ p (p ∨ ¬p)` with `var p; prop p` was
; accepted (sound, over the two truth values, but used by no file); now statements are neither
; objects nor the range of a quantifier (doc/kurt-ref.md §5.1).
load logic, equality
var p
prop p
expect "TypeError" "a binder ranges over terms"
    use ∀ p (p ∨ ¬p)
expect "TypeError" "a binder ranges over terms"
    use ∀ %A (%A ∨ ¬%A)
expect "TypeError" "a binder ranges over terms"
    use ∃ q (q ∧ true)
expect "TypeError" "a binder ranges over terms"
    use ∀ r r
use %A ∨ ¬%A  "lem"
use ∀ x (x = x)
prop P
arity P 1
use ∀ x (P x ∨ ¬P x)
